# .nancy-ignore — Sonatype OSS Index vulnerability suppressions
#
# FORMAT: one CVE / SONATYPE ID per line, optionally followed by a comment.
# IDs come from nancy output (e.g. "CVE-2021-12345" or "sonatype-2021-1234").
# Entries here suppress matching findings in `nancy sleuth` so the build does not
# fail on known-acceptable risks.
#
# SUPPRESSION PROCESS
# -------------------
# 1. Run `make vuln-scan` (or the CI job) — note the finding ID(s).
# 2. Open a tracking issue: "vuln: suppress <ID> — <reason>".
# 3. Gather evidence:
#    a. Is the vulnerable code path reachable in our binary?  (govulncheck
#       already filters unreachable callgraphs; nancy does not — so manual
#       review is required here.)
#    b. Is a fix available? If yes, prefer upgrading the dependency over
#       suppressing.
#    c. CVSS score ≥ 7.0 (HIGH) or ≥ 9.0 (CRITICAL) — suppression requires
#       explicit sign-off from a maintainer in the tracking issue.
# 4. Add the ID below with: date, tracking issue URL, and a one-line rationale.
# 5. Set a review-by date (max 90 days). Re-evaluate at that point.
#
# EXAMPLE (do not uncomment — illustrative only):
# CVE-2021-44228  # log4shell — not in Go; false positive. Issue #42. Review: 2026-06-01
#
# --- active suppressions (none yet) ---
